{"results":[{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000076","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The full text describes an auto-encoder with an explicit decoder and generative sampling, trained self-supervised on a large protein corpus. It also reports task-agnostic generation and transfer across protein families.","evidence_snippet":"“support generative sampling” and “a one-step recycling iteration ... improves quality and diversity”"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000082","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The record describes a transfer-learning framework for universal cell embeddings, not a generative model. It does show broad pretrained language-model embeddings and cross-species transfer.","evidence_snippet":"“learns universal cell embeddings” by combining RNA expression with embeddings from protein language models and general-purpose language models"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000106","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"scMIR is presented as a pretrained vision-language representation model with reconstruction and alignment modules, but the outputs are task-agnostic embeddings rather than generated outputs. The evidence supports foundation-model-like pretraining and broad applicability.","evidence_snippet":"“pre-trained on 207,957 image-text pairs” and “outputs task-agnostic image embeddings”"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000131","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a training and reasoning framework around an LLM policy, with teacher-generated CoT data, rather than evidence of a new broadly pretrained foundation model. The model itself is described as generating responses autoregressively.","evidence_snippet":"“the model outputs a textual response y generated autoregressively according to the policy”"}]}
